(PAPER-TO-WORLD / AUTHORED DEMONSTRATION NOTES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One neuron in three dimensions: demonstration notes) Tj T*
(Page 1: Meet a neuron in 3D.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Background teaching material. Not a published research paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Before a neuron sends a signal, it holds a quiet electrical difference across its) Tj T*
(membrane.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In this model, that resting potential is -65 millivolts; without an input, the) Tj T*
(voltage stays there.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Rotate the schematic neuron to see its branching inputs, cell body, and myelinated) Tj T*
(axon.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Parameters throughout these notes: rest/reset = -65 mV; resistance = 10 Mohm;) Tj T*
(default tau = 20 ms. A resting neuron starts at V = -65 mV. I is applied current in) Tj T*
(nA. These are illustrative model choices, not empirical measurements. The 3D) Tj T*
(anatomy is schematic. Dendrites are drawn as branching inputs, the soma as the cell) Tj T*
(body, and six myelin sheaths around the axon. Geometry and myelin do not affect) Tj T*
(this single-compartment model.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At rest with I = 0, both the input and the voltage difference from rest are zero.) Tj T*
(There is no net change, so the model remains at -65 mV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Membrane: The boundary that holds the voltage difference.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dendrites / input: The branching input tree. The slider applies one lumped input) Tj T*
(current to the model, not a separate current in each branch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Axon: The output path that carries the neuron's signal away from its cell body.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Myelin: Insulating sheaths illustrated around the axon. Their geometry does not) Tj T*
(change this single-compartment calculation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
