BT /F1 10 Tf 15.00 TL 48 748 Td
(PAPER-TO-WORLD / AUTHORED DEMONSTRATION NOTES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One neuron in three dimensions: demonstration notes) Tj T*
(Page 2: Input arrives at the dendrites.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Background teaching material. Not a published research paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Input collects in the branching dendrites and flows into the cell body, the soma.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the soma the input charges the membrane while a leak pulls it back toward rest;) Tj T*
(the time constant sets how fast it settles.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Differential equation: tau * dV/dt = -\(V - Vrest\) + R*I. Numerical method: forward) Tj T*
(Euler, dt = 0.1 ms. At each step, V += \(-\(V+65\)+10*I\)/tau * 0.1. Equilibrium: Vrest) Tj T*
(+ R*I. There is no stochastic input. One voltage represents the whole neuron. This) Tj T*
(is not a spatial cable model. Branches and membrane pores illustrate the lesson,) Tj T*
(not individually simulated compartments or ion channels.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(With R = 10 Mohm the voltage settles at Vrest + RI = -65 + 10 = -55 mV. There the) Tj T*
(leak exactly balances the input, so it stays below the -50 mV threshold.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dendrites: The branching input tree. The slider applies one lumped input current to) Tj T*
(the model, not a separate current in each branch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Soma: The cell body. Its single membrane voltage stands for the whole neuron in) Tj T*
(this model.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Leak: The tendency for the membrane voltage to move back toward rest.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
