(PAPER-TO-WORLD / AUTHORED DEMONSTRATION NOTES) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(One neuron in three dimensions: demonstration notes) Tj T*
(Page 3: The trigger zone decides.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Background teaching material. Not a published research paper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Where the axon leaves the soma, the trigger zone watches the membrane voltage.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When it reaches -50 mV the model emits a spike, resets to -65 mV and holds there) Tj T*
(for 2 ms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(After the Euler voltage update, if V >= -50 mV: increment spike count; set V = -65) Tj T*
(mV; set refractory timer = 2 ms. While that timer is positive, decrement it by dt) Tj T*
(\(clamped at zero\) and hold V = -65 mV. A +20 mV graphical marker records an event,) Tj T*
(not an action-potential waveform. Each spike triggers a 60 ms illustrative transit) Tj T*
(animation along the 3D axon. This duration is a visualization choice, not a) Tj T*
(computed or measured conduction speed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(At 1.4 nA the voltage settles at -65 + 14 = -51 mV and never reaches -50 mV. In) Tj T*
(this model the input must exceed 1.5 nA to fire.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trigger zone: The axon hillock, drawn where the axon begins. The model fires when) Tj T*
(the voltage reaches -50 mV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Spike: A discrete output event: a pulse leaves the trigger zone and travels along) Tj T*
(the axon.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Reset: After a spike, voltage returns to -65 mV before integration resumes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
endstream
